    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. we've been having some issues with the top layers feeling a bit shaky though, even when the base is heavy. sometimes it feels like the weight shifts unexpectedly during transit or just sitting there. any specific tips on how to secure the load better so it doesn't tip or slide around?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To address top-layer shifting, consider using load securement devices like corner boards or specialized edge protectors on the pallets themselves. For palletized loads, shrink-wrapping tightly around the entire pallet unit adds significant lateral stability against swaying. If loads are exceptionally high or unstable, utilizing specialized plastic or metal restraints designed for racking can prevent sliding between tiers. Proper load configuration and secure wrapping are key to minimizing unexpected movement.",
      "source": "target",
